// expected: cannot concatenate value of type
//
// '|' concatenates when EITHER side is text and is the bitwise OR otherwise, so
// a text/other MIX is a type error. stage4 emitted the concatenation anyway and
// clang rejected the module with
//
//     '%t7' defined with type 'i64' but expected '{ ptr, i64, i64 }'
//       %cc4 = extractvalue {ptr, i64, i64} %t7, 0
//
// which names no source line, no type and no operator. The fix reports the mix
// where it is written, and points at .String(), which is the idiom this tree
// uses for every builtin (string and []byte are one type in Moxie, so TextType
// covers both spellings and `"a" | []byte("b")` stays legal).
package main

func main() {
	var a int64 = 5
	println("x=" | a)
}
